[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2980B9]Design Philosophy[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[B]Function over form.[/B] No GUI, no flashy commands — plain YAML files you can version-control and diff. Every behavior is configurable, but the defaults are sane.

[B]Nuanced setup, extreme flexibility.[/B] Teleportation is controlled by [I]regions[/I] — yaml files you can hot-reload via command. Per-region: shape, radius, center, curve weighting, vertical bounds, sky-light check, world permission, unique placements, region expansion, and a fallback world if the player lacks permission. RTP also exposes events, interchangeable shapes, and an addon API so you can integrate with custom generators, claim plugins, or your own logic.

[B]Designed for SMP and small networks first.[/B] That's where this functionality is most needed; that's where it's tested hardest.

[CENTER][COLOR=#D1D1D1]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#16A085]Platform Support[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]✅ [B][COLOR=#27AE60]Paper[/COLOR][/B] — fully async chunk loading via native `getChunkAtAsync`. The recommended setup.
[*]✅ [B][COLOR=#27AE60]Paper forks[/COLOR][/B] — [B]Leaf[/B], [B]Leaves[/B], [B]Purpur[/B], [B]Pufferfish[/B], [B]Airplane[/B], and other Paper-derived forks are supported on the Paper code path; they inherit Paper-class async chunk loading. Use the Paper/Spigot build of RTP. ([I][B]Leaf[/B] and [B]Leaves[/B] are separate projects despite the similar names.[/I])
[*]✅ [B][COLOR=#E67E22]Spigot[/COLOR][/B] — supported. Region files (`.mca`) are parsed off-tick to skip bad candidates [I]before[/I] a chunk load is needed, so most `/rtp` calls feel Paper-class even on vanilla Spigot.
[*]✅ [B][COLOR=#E67E22]Spigot forks[/COLOR][/B] — Spigot-derived forks without the Paper async chunk API run the Spigot code path (Anvil pre-filter + bounded main-thread fallback).
[*]🌱 [B][COLOR=#7F8C8D]Custom generators[/COLOR][/B] — Iris, Terra, datapack-driven worlds — work out of the box. Modded biome and block IDs are preserved.
[*]❌ [B][COLOR=#C0392B]Folia[/COLOR][/B] — [B]not bundled in Lite[/B]. Folia operators must use [B]RTP-Pro[/B], which ships the Folia adapter (Region Scheduler, off-tick safety pre-filter, no 1-tick stalls).
[*]✅ [B][COLOR=#27AE60]Mohist / Arclight[/COLOR][/B] — officially supported Bukkit-compatibility launchers for Forge / NeoForge servers. Use the Spigot/Paper build of RTP; the Spigot code path applies. This is the recommended way to run RTP on a Forge or NeoForge server.
[*]🚧 [B][COLOR=#C0392B]Fabric[/COLOR][/B] — adapter ships in-tree but `/rtp` is [B]not functional[/B] yet. Planned for a later release.
[*]🔁 [B][COLOR=#C0392B]Native Forge / NeoForge[/COLOR][/B] — no native adapter planned. Use [B]Arclight[/B] or [B]Mohist[/B] above.
[/LIST]

[B]Best setup:[/B] Paper, with memory to spare for the pre-generation queue. RTP works particularly well on servers that have already been pre-generated.

[CENTER][COLOR=#D1D1D1]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#2C3E50]Performance vs. Other RTP Plugins[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[I]How RTP (Lite) and RTP-Pro stack up against the most-deployed RTP plugins on the three Bukkit-family server architectures. Folia is the clearest delta between the two tiers — Lite drops the Folia adapter, Pro ships it. Both rows are shown so you can see what upgrading would change.[/I]

[B]Confidence legend:[/B] 🧪 = measured locally on the RTP benchmark harness · 📖 = read from the plugin's published docs / resource page · ❓ = inferred from the plugin's known architecture, not yet verified.

[B]Architecture support matrix[/B]
[TABLE]
[TR][TD][B]Plugin[/B][/TD][TD][B]Spigot[/B][/TD][TD][B]Paper (and forks)[/B][/TD][TD][B]Folia[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]RTP (Lite)[/B][/TD][TD]✅ 🧪 Off-tick Anvil pre-filter; rare bounded main-thread fallback.[/TD][TD]✅ 🧪 Fully async via native `getChunkAtAsync`; no fallback path.[/TD][TD]❌ Folia adapter not bundled in Lite — see [B]RTP-Pro[/B].[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]RTP-Pro[/B][/TD][TD]✅ 🧪 Same Spigot path as Lite.[/TD][TD]✅ 🧪 Same Paper path as Lite.[/TD][TD]✅ 🧪 Region Scheduler + off-tick pre-filter; no 1-tick stalls.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]BetterRTP[/TD][TD]⚠️ 📖 Synchronous chunk load on miss; TPS spikes during generation are widely reported.[/TD][TD]⚠️ 📖 Uses Paper async where available, but no off-tick safety pre-filter.[/TD][TD]❌ 📖 No native Folia adapter; runs on Paper-compat fork only.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]EzRTP[/TD][TD]❌ 🧪 Loads on Spigot 1.20.1 but its async update-checker throws `NoSuchMethodError` on the Paper-only `JavaPlugin#getPluginMeta()` ([I]SpigotUpdateChecker:28[/I]); core path otherwise statistics-driven, no Anvil pre-filter — sync chunk load on miss.[/TD][TD]✅ 📖 Built-in percentile/timing metrics on Paper.[/TD][TD]❓ 📖 Not advertised as Folia-aware.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]AsyRTP[/TD][TD]❌ 🧪 Fails to enable on Spigot 1.20.1 — `StartupBanner.print` calls the Paper-only `JavaPlugin#getPluginMeta()` during `onEnable`, throwing `NoSuchMethodError` before the plugin initializes. Effectively Paper/Folia-only despite the name.[/TD][TD]✅ 📖 Async location search.[/TD][TD]✅ 📖 Region-thread-safe; explicit Folia target.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]SorekillRTP[/TD][TD]⚠️ ❓ Functional, but the design centre is Redis-backed cross-server, not single-server perf.[/TD][TD]⚠️ ❓ Same.[/TD][TD]❓ 📖 Folia compatibility not specifically documented.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]AdvancedRTP[/TD][TD]⚠️ 📖 Safety-first; trades speed for ground/biome detection. Sync chunk load on candidate evaluation.[/TD][TD]⚠️ 📖 Same path on Paper.[/TD][TD]❌ 📖 No documented Folia support.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]JakesRTP[/TD][TD]⚠️ 📖 Async via `prefer-sync-tp: false`; configurable destination cache (`cache-locations`).[/TD][TD]✅ 📖 Same async path on Paper; widely deployed.[/TD][TD]❌ 📖 No native Folia adapter (community forks vary).[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]EssentialsX `/rtp`[/TD][TD]✅ 📖 Works; main-thread chunk load on each candidate.[/TD][TD]✅ 📖 Works; same path, no async chunk API use.[/TD][TD]❌ 📖 Folia not supported by EssentialsX core.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]HuskHomes RTP[/TD][TD]✅ 📖 Works; bundled with the broader homes/teleport suite.[/TD][TD]✅ 📖 Same path on Paper.[/TD][TD]❓ 📖 Partial — see HuskHomes' own platform matrix.[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

